course: dictionary
lesson: 11355
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Zombie is one of them. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: In a story or game, a zombie is a made-up dead person who walks slowly without thinking. But look at this: «They finally drop off at three and spend Sunday as grumpy zombies.» The children are not dead. They are very tired, so zombie means half-asleep and not thinking clearly.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. "They spend Sunday as grumpy, half-asleep people" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Zombies in films and games are fiction, not fact.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A zombie can be a made-up dead person from stories, films and games. Zombies are not real.
fact: Informally, «zombie» can mean a person who is very tired and moves without thinking, as in «I'm a zombie in the mornings».
fact: Zombie can also describe something that keeps going when it should have ended, such as a zombie company.
fact: Zombie is a noun (a zombie, zombies) and an adjective in phrases like zombie film and zombie mode.
exercise: «They finally drop off at three and spend Sunday as grumpy zombies.» What does zombie mean here? | A made-up dead person who walks slowly | A zombie film on television | A monster in a Halloween costume | *Very tired and half-asleep
exercise: In a Halloween game, what is a zombie? | A company that has failed | A tired person who needs a nap | A loud noise at night | *A made-up dead person from stories and games
exercise: Mum says, «That old club is a zombie: it should have closed years ago but it keeps going.» What does zombie mean here? | A very tired person | A quiet, sleepy place | *Something that keeps going when it should have ended | A made-up monster from films
test: «I'm a zombie in the mornings until I've had my toast.» What does zombie mean? | Someone who loves films about monsters | *Very tired and not thinking clearly | A tall, scary monster | A dead person who has come back to life
test: Which is the correct sentence about zombies? | *Zombies are made-up monsters in stories, films and games | Zombies are real, and you can meet them at the zoo | Zombies are a kind of bird that sleeps all day | Zombies are famous dancers
exam: Jade reads, «The zombie project has no money and no plan, yet the team still meets every week.» Why is zombie a good word here? | It means a Halloween costume | It means the team is dead | *It shows the project keeps going even though it should have ended | It shows the team is very tired
